  "id": "pr-277",
  "instruction": "Extend the glom command-line interface so it can load target data as TOML in addition to its existing JSON, YAML, and Python formats. TOML targets must work consistently whether supplied through the existing argument-based interface, read from a file, or read from standard input, and the loaded data must then be usable as the target for the existing glom transformation/spec execution flow. Preserve the current behavior and syntax for the other supported formats. The CLI must clearly report usage errors, including missing or invalid command-line arguments, unsupported or ambiguous target formats, malformed TOML (and other input data), and unusable specs, by returning a nonzero status and an actionable error on stderr rather than silently producing an incorrect result or an unhandled traceback. Help and normal successful invocations must continue to behave as expected, and TOML output/input handling must not change the established result format of the CLI.",
